  strengths: [
    "The final RHP shows a substantial 61-store South Indian footprint, long operating history and FY26 revenue above ₹25,000 crore.",
    "FY26 operating EBITDA more than doubled and PAT increased 177%, with EBITDA margin rising to 6.69% and ROCE to 42.60%.",
    "High reported revenue per store indicates strong throughput at mature locations, although gold price and bullion mix affect comparability.",
    "₹1,033.23 crore of fresh proceeds is tied directly to inventory and fit-out for 10 new stores, making deployment measurable after listing.",
  ],
  concerns: [
    "Inventory reached ₹9,816.28 crore, or 89.7% of FY26 assets, and operating cash flow was negative ₹397.76 crore despite ₹1,009.82 crore PAT. The ₹998.68 crore offer-funded inventory equals about 10.2% of the FY26 inventory base and arrives before the 10 new stores establish throughput.",
    "Borrowings rose to ₹1,604.14 crore in FY26 from ₹949.26 crore in FY25; outstanding borrowings were ₹1,238.10 crore at 30 June 2026.",
    "The ₹1,604.14 crore borrowing figure excludes ₹441.26 crore of FY26 lease liabilities. Cash lease payments were ₹90.21 crore in FY26, so store economics and leverage should also be assessed after lease cash outflows rather than from debt ratios alone.",
    "Gold jewellery contributed 92.33% of FY26 revenue and procurement is concentrated. Gold-price movements can affect consumer demand, reported sales, collateral and margins.",
    "Customer purchase-scheme advances were ₹5,042.75 crore, or 20.15% of FY26 revenue, and increased 60.3% year on year. These customer-funded liabilities must be matched by inventory, redemption capacity and liquidity rather than treated as ordinary free working capital.",
    "Scheme advances have risen 159.5% since FY24, versus 49.1% growth in revenue over the same period. The gap does not establish a shortfall by itself, but it increases the importance of maturity matching, redemption behaviour and unrestricted liquidity alongside the ₹8,683.03 crore gold inventory balance.",
    "The two disclosed schemes mature after 11 monthly instalments and include either a cash-equivalent bonus or a discount on value-addition charges. Those incentives make the ₹5,042.75 crore advance balance an operating obligation with both redemption timing and fulfilment-margin effects, not a cost-free deposit base.",
    "The company says it does not use gold-metal loans, forward contracts or options to hedge gold-price exposure. That leaves the ₹9,816.28 crore inventory base directly exposed to price, demand and replenishment timing risk.",
    "Gold, silver and diamond inventory is valued at the lower of net realisable value and annual weighted-average cost. In a fast-moving bullion market, that averaging convention can make reported gross margin and any later write-down sensitive to purchase timing, product ageing and the selling-price assumptions used in net realisable value.",
    "The RHP's insurance table reports only 81.04% coverage against its stated FY26 asset base, down from 110.11% in FY25. Some policies are in promoter M. Kiran Kumar Jain's name, making the company dependent on him for related claims; policy exclusions, deductibles and the different denominator from restated consolidated assets limit any inference about inventory protection.",
    "The company has identified cities but has not selected precise sites or signed binding agreements for the 10 funded stores. Security deposits, advance rentals and cost overruns are outside the ₹1,033.23 crore offer allocation and must be funded from internal accruals.",
    "Tamil Nadu supplied 53.98% of FY26 revenue and eight of the 10 proposed stores are in that state. The new capital therefore deepens, rather than reduces, dependence on one regional demand, competition and regulatory environment.",
    "FY26 employee attrition was 30.90%, including 33.83% in sales and 38.98% in administration. Managing 10 store openings while retaining frontline and control staff is an execution risk alongside the inventory build.",
    "The FY26 auditor found that the audit-trail feature in the JILABA system used for sales and inventory did not operate throughout the year. Because the feature was not enabled, the auditor could not comment on tampering or preservation for that system; this is material beside ₹9,816.28 crore of inventory.",
    "The final RHP reports 197 delayed statutory-payment instances involving ₹2.80 crore in FY26, 355 involving ₹5.11 crore in FY25 and 327 involving ₹22.43 crore in FY24, led by professional tax and TDS. It states no amounts were delayed for GST or provident fund in those years.",
    "Some historical RoC forms, resolutions, share-transfer deeds and other corporate records are untraceable. The company has relied on alternative records and company-secretary certificates; a June 2024 PAS-3 clerical error was re-filed in May 2025, and the RHP says no RoC action had begun by its date.",
    "The RHP reports six company tax proceedings involving ₹56.04 crore and one criminal plus seven tax proceedings involving promoters, with promoter tax exposure of ₹27.02 crore. Outcomes remain uncertain.",
    "SEBI had issued summons to promoter M. Kiran Kumar Jain in 2022 in connection with Krishana Fabrics; the RHP says no further communication or action had been received as of its date.",
    "A prior related-party brand-ambassador fee reached ₹50.28 crore in FY24. Although the arrangement ended, promoter remuneration and related-party governance warrant continued review.",
    "Promoters are expected to retain roughly 82–83% after the offer. That preserves operating continuity but leaves public shareholders with limited influence over board appointments, related-party approvals and capital allocation.",
  ],
